{"ghsa_id":"GHSA-823j-m4cj-hmjf","cve_id":null,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/security-advisories/GHSA-823j-m4cj-hmjf","html_url":"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/security/advisories/GHSA-823j-m4cj-hmjf","summary":"MOSS-Audio request-controlled processor cache permits remote memory exhaustion","description":"### Summary\r\n\r\n  When vLLM serves a MOSS-Audio model, a client that can access the /tokenize endpoint can provide request-controlled\r\n  mm_processor_kwargs.\r\n\r\n  MOSS-Audio uses these values to construct MossAudioProcessor instances and stores every distinct instance in an\r\n  unbounded private dictionary. Each processor contains a WhisperFeatureExtractor with an allocated mel-filter array.\r\n\r\n  An attacker can therefore:\r\n\r\n  1. Repeatedly submit distinct processor configurations to cause persistent linear memory growth.\r\n  2. Supply oversized mel_config values to amplify the allocation made by a single request.\r\n\r\n  This can exhaust host memory and terminate or severely degrade the API process. /tokenize is intentionally outside\r\n  vLLM’s API-key-protected route prefixes, so --api-key alone does not restrict access to this endpoint.\r\n\r\n  ### Details\r\n\r\n  TokenizeChatRequest accepts arbitrary mm_processor_kwargs\r\n  (https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/bf7eee9d7b2788bafe69f0c21fde6af22a2d3319/vllm/entrypoints/serve/tokenize/protocol.py#L107-L110).\r\n\r\n  The request reaches multimodal processing through:\r\n\r\n  1. ServingTokenization.create_tokenize()\r\n\r\n     (https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/bf7eee9d7b2788bafe69f0c21fde6af22a2d3319/vllm/entrypoints/serve/tokenize/serving.py#L84-L92)\r\n\r\n  2. OnlineRenderer.preprocess_chat()\r\n\r\n     (https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/bf7eee9d7b2788bafe69f0c21fde6af22a2d3319/vllm/renderers/online_renderer.py#L675-L704)\r\n\r\n  3. BaseRenderer._process_multimodal()\r\n\r\n     (https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/bf7eee9d7b2788bafe69f0c21fde6af22a2d3319/vllm/renderers/base.py#L846-L880)\r\n\r\n  4. MossAudioMultiModalProcessor._apply_hf_processor_main()\r\n\r\n     (https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/bf7eee9d7b2788bafe69f0c21fde6af22a2d3319/vllm/model_executor/models/moss_audio.py#L1358-L1400)\r\n\r\n  Although /tokenize sets skip_mm_cache=True, this only selects the read-only multimodal processor. Its\r\n  MossAudioProcessingInfo object still maintains the vulnerable private cache.\r\n\r\n  The following request-controlled fields are used as cache-key components:\r\n\r\n  - audio_token_id\r\n  - audio_start_id\r\n  - audio_end_id\r\n  - enable_time_marker\r\n  - mel_config\r\n\r\n  MossAudioProcessingInfo.get_hf_processor()\r\n  (https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/bf7eee9d7b2788bafe69f0c21fde6af22a2d3319/vllm/model_executor/models/moss_audio.py#L1248-L1304)\r\n  creates _hf_processor_cache as a plain dictionary. It has no capacity limit, TTL, or eviction policy.\r\n\r\n  For every new key, it constructs a MossAudioProcessor\r\n  (https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/bf7eee9d7b2788bafe69f0c21fde6af22a2d3319/vllm/model_executor/models/moss_audio.py#L962-L997),\r\n  which creates a WhisperFeatureExtractor.\r\n\r\n  The default mel-filter array has:\r\n\r\n  shape: (201, 128)\r\n  dtype: float64\r\n  size: 205,824 bytes\r\n\r\n  Consequently, each unique default configuration retains approximately 206 KB in the mel-filter array alone.\r\n\r\n  Request-controlled mel_config can amplify this substantially. The bounded configuration:\r\n\r\n  {\r\n    \"mel_dim\": 512,\r\n    \"mel_n_fft\": 1024\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  creates:\r\n\r\n  shape: (513, 512)\r\n  dtype: float64\r\n  size: 2,101,248 bytes\r\n\r\n  The approximate final mel-filter allocation is:\r\n\r\n  (floor(mel_n_fft / 2) + 1) * mel_dim * 8 bytes\r\n\r\n  There are no effective upper bounds on these values. For example, mel_dim=65536 and mel_n_fft=65536 would attempt to\r\n  allocate approximately 16 GiB for the final mel-filter array alone. This destructive value was not executed.\r\n\r\n  Clearing the normal multimodal processor cache does not clear _hf_processor_cache, so these processors remain\r\n  reachable for the lifetime of the frontend process.\r\n\r\n  The project’s security documentation\r\n  (https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/bf7eee9d7b2788bafe69f0c21fde6af22a2d3319/docs/usage/security.md#L185-L214)\r\n  documents /tokenize as an endpoint that does not require an API key.\r\n\r\n  Suggested remediation is to reject request-level overrides of processor-construction parameters, validate strict upper\r\n  bounds for mel dimensions, and either eliminate this dynamic cache or replace it with a small bounded cache that is\r\n  also cleared by cache-reset operations.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n  ### Impact\r\n\r\n  An attacker who can reach a vLLM HTTP server serving a MOSS-Audio model can cause persistent attacker-controlled\r\n  memory allocations in the frontend API process.\r\n\r\n  Repeated unique configurations cause linear retained-memory growth. Oversized mel_config values can also cause a very\r\n  large allocation from a single request. Continued exploitation can terminate the process through out-of-memory\r\n  exhaustion, resulting in denial of service.\r\n\r\n  The issue is limited to deployments serving a MOSS-Audio model. A reverse proxy that authenticates or rate-limits /\r\n  tokenize can reduce exposure, but vLLM’s own --api-key setting does not protect this endpoint.","severity":"high","author":null,"publisher":{"login":"jperezdealgaba","id":124347725,"node_id":"U_kgDOB2llTQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/124347725?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jperezdealgaba","html_url":"https://github.com/jperezdealgaba","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jperezdealgaba/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jperezdealgaba/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jperezdealgaba/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jperezdealgaba/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jperezdealgaba/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jperezdealgaba/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jperezdealgaba/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jperezdealgaba/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jperezdealgaba/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"identifiers":[{"value":"GHSA-823j-m4cj-hmjf","type":"GHSA"}],"state":"published","created_at":null,"updated_at":"2026-10-06T06:59:51Z","published_at":"2026-10-06T06:59:51Z","closed_at":null,"withdrawn_at":null,"submission":null,"vulnerabilities":[{"package":{"ecosystem":"pip","name":"vllm"},"vulnerable_version_range":"> 0.24.0, < 0.31.0","patched_versions":">= 0.31.0","vulnerable_functions":[]}],"cvss_severities":{"cvss_v3":{"vector_string":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","score":7.5},"cvss_v4":{"vector_string":null,"score":null}},"cwes":[{"cwe_id":"CWE-770","name":"Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling"}],"cwe_ids":["CWE-770"],"credits":[{"login":"dohashelby","type":"reporter"},{"login":"DarkLight1337","type":"remediation_reviewer"},{"login":"jperezdealgaba","type":"coordinator"}],"credits_detailed":[{"user":{"login":"dohashelby","id":244447911,"node_id":"U_kgDODpH6pw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244447911?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dohashelby","html_url":"https://github.com/dohashelby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dohashelby/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dohashelby/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dohashelby/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dohashelby/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dohashelby/s